    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>The Fief du Nord spans the Lille-Roubaix-Tourcoing conurbation out to the Channel ports of Calais and Dunkirk. Once a stronghold of conservative industrialist Ventrue, it passed after the Second World War into the hands of &Eacute;tienne, a Brujah Marquis &mdash; one of the rare Camarilla Fiefs actually ruled by that Clan. An idealist revolutionary turned reluctant ruler, &Eacute;tienne is deeply unpopular even among his own Clan, who accuse him of selling out to the Parisian Toreador; he prefers the title Tribune to Marquis and has held power for half a century thanks to distant Princely support and his enemies' inability to unite against him.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Weary, pragmatic, uncomfortable in the role of ruler. You wanted revolution, not a throne, and every year in power costs you a little more of your old convictions.</p>",
    "notes": "Rules under Provost Crevel's shadow, who is widely believed the Fief's true second power. Rivals Reynier (Idealist opposition) and Ianka (Anarch icon) within his own clan.",
